    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2443bf72_b131865a",
        "filename": "chip/g/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-04T16:02:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that changing BID flags to test prepvt images is good.  Especially if more Cr50 prod releases are skipped in the future.\nIs there a need for setting the BID as well with an SQA image?  I\u0027ve heard that some ODMs have misprogrammed the BID in the past, which currently requires a DBG image to recover.",
      "parentUuid": "26f75d2b_e0aebb8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "e1a3e6d2f902e692400aa4d207c13044a7173d0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "faa2ecf4_ae89f224",
        "filename": "chip/g/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-04T16:19:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They have set the board ids incorrectly in the past, but the issue with those incorrect board ids is always the flags. The flags lockout certain images and early stage boards sometimes need to run prepvt images. The RLZ part of the board id doesn\u0027t really affect cr50 very much so there\u0027s no real need to change the RLZ part.",
      "parentUuid": "2443bf72_b131865a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "e1a3e6d2f902e692400aa4d207c13044a7173d0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c39f6c04_784c9549",
        "filename": "chip/g/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-04T21:11:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think for now we should set the flags to 0xffffffff and keep the force_pvt support in bid.",
      "parentUuid": "faa2ecf4_ae89f224",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "e1a3e6d2f902e692400aa4d207c13044a7173d0a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96f49598_2023cdf6",
        "filename": "chip/g/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-04T21:20:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having thought about it a bit more:\n\nI don\u0027t think it is worth having two different commands for this pocess, and there is no strong case for setting board ID flags to all ones.\n\nOn top of that note that we are not going to build generic images with this flag set anyways, those will be strictly one offs on the as need basis.\n\nIf a need to set flags arises we can modify this function to allow setting flags field. Still would be better than having two functions.",
      "parentUuid": "c39f6c04_784c9549",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 33
